{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/squinlan/artifact-classifier","sessionId":"01bba593-0ced-45e4-9217-f199cf74c606","version":"2.0.60","gitBranch":"main","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<ide_opened_file>The user opened the file /home/squinlan/cull-context-assembler/api.md in the IDE. This may or may not be related to the current task.</ide_opened_file>"},{"type":"text","text":"You are reviewing the documentation for **Cull**, a deterministic discard-based context assembler service. This is part of a multi-service architecture that includes:\n\n- **Artifact Engine** (Python, port 3002) - Registry-based document storage\n- **Turnstile** (Node backend port 3001, React frontend port 5173) - Turn-centric conversation interface\n- **Cull** (Python, port 3003) - Context assembly for LLM prompts\n\n## Your Tasks\n\n1. **Review the documentation** in `/home/squinlan/cull-context-assembler/` for completeness, consistency, and clarity\n\n2. **Verify Artifact Engine integration** - Cull's `content_providers.md` defines an expected Artifact Engine API. Compare this against the actual Artifact Engine API spec at `/home/squinlan/artifact-engine/docs/api_spec_v1.md`. Note any mismatches and propose adapter code.\n\n3. **Normalize the project** to match sibling projects:\n   - Create a `docs/` subdirectory and move the .md files there\n   - Create a README.md with project summary and doc index\n   - Create a .gitignore for Python development\n   - Initialize git repo if not present\n   - Ensure document headers use consistent format: `# Cull: <Title>`\n\n4. **Check naming consistency**:\n   - Project name should be \"Cull\" throughout (not \"Cull Context Assembler\" in headers)\n   - Service name in headers: `**Service Name:** cull`\n   - Port 3003 should be consistent across all docs\n\n5. **Cross-reference with Turnstile** - Turnstile's backend_architecture.md references a \"baby assembler\" for context. Cull is the full implementation. Note if Turnstile docs should reference Cull or if they're intentionally separate.\n\n## Reference Documents\n\nRead these first to understand the ecosystem:\n- `/home/squinlan/artifact-engine/docs/api_spec_v1.md` - Artifact Engine's actual API\n- `/home/squinlan/turnstile/docs/backend_architecture.md` - Shows how Turnstile assembles context\n\n## Style Guide (from sibling projects)\n\n- Document headers: `# ProjectName: Document Title`\n- Metadata block: `**Project:** X`, `**Status:** Draft`, `**Last Updated:** December 2025`\n- Section numbers: `## 1. Title`, `## 2. Title`\n- Code blocks with language tags\n- Tables for comparison data\n- File map section linking to other docs\n- `*Next: ...` footer linking to next doc\nKey issues I spotted that the new session should address:\nAPI mismatch - Cull expects /artifacts and /artifacts/batch endpoints that don't exist in Artifact Engine. The actual API uses:\nPOST /artifact/search (not GET /artifacts)\nGET /artifact/{id}/content (not GET /artifacts/{id})\nNo batch endpoint exists\nFolder structure - Docs are in root, should be in docs/\nNo README or .gitignore\nHeader inconsistency - Uses \"Cull Context Assembler:\" should be \"Cull:\""}]},"uuid":"878f1938-694d-434d-b7e0-c5b7a915704f","timestamp":"2025-12-07T00:34:54.862Z"}
